CRASH-06: require at least two points on a GPV head loss curve

curvecoeff() finds the curve segment that brackets the flow. A curve
with one point has no segment, so it read X[-1] and Y[-1] (or X[1] and
Y[1]) of a one-element array. validatecurves() only requires one point,
which is enough for a pump curve but not for a GPV. Extend
validatevalves() (added by CRASH-16) to report a GPV curve with fewer
than two points as error 231, so EN_openH returns 110.

Requires: CRASH-16

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb, after CRASH-16:
    git apply CRASH-16_fix.patch
    git apply CRASH-06_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/validate.c b/src/validate.c
index f56d848..da1b73c 100644
--- a/src/validate.c
+++ b/src/validate.c
@@ -179,6 +179,16 @@ int validatevalves(Project *pr)
             writeline(pr, pr->Msg);
             result = 0;
         }
+
+        // Head loss is interpolated between curve points, so a GPV's
+        // curve needs at least 2 (validatecurves() reports 0 points)
+        else if (net->Curve[c].Npts == 1)
+        {
+            sprintf(pr->Msg, "Error 231: %s %s (a GPV curve needs 2 or more points)",
+                geterrmsg(231, errmsg), net->Curve[c].ID);
+            writeline(pr, pr->Msg);
+            result = 0;
+        }
     }
     return result;
 }
